  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political landscape in Indonesia is currently focused on the succession of the vice presidential office following the departure of Gibran Rakabuming Raka. President Prabowo Subianto has confirmed that the process of selecting a replacement is being conducted through democratic channels, noting that he personally chose the two candidates submitted for consideration. Among the figures reported to be under consideration are Sugiono and Amran Sulaiman, both of whom possess records of government service. While the Gerindra Party has formally expressed its unified support for Sugiono, other potential candidates like Amran Sulaiman have stated they are leaving the final decision to fate. The administration is reportedly prioritizing specific criteria for the new vice president, including long-term loyalty and the capability to implement national policy effectively. The president has remarked that the current situation regarding this leadership change was previously unforeseen.",
